module gunbc.plans.claim_execution_consolidation

import std.dissolution { unbound_dissolution }
import gunbc.plan { Plan, PlanRetiresWhen, PlanIsAuthorityOnly }
import std.markdown { MarkdownBlock }
import gunbc.markdown_helpers { h2, p, li, ul, ol, quote }

fn claim_execution_consolidation_body() -> List<MarkdownBlock> {
  [
    quote(blocks: [
      p(text: "**This plan is written as an intention** (`gunbc.design_argument::plans_are_intentions`): what the repository should become, why, and done-when. How it is realized is downstream; the work items that realize it name this plan and are not listed here."),
      p(text: "**Grounding:** `gunbc.design_argument::single_authority` (one meaning of a claim result), `gunbc.design_argument::root_generalization` (three entrypoints are leaves of one rule), `gunbc.design_argument::replacement_migration` (the old entrypoints end in one motion, the survivor never falls back to them, and where the survivor cannot yet hold a required boundary the old structure stays frozen), `gunbc.design_argument::consumption` (a spelling no executing caller passes is not carried forward), `gunbc.design_argument::fail_closed` (completeness is an identity join, not a count equality). The operator's choice of this direction is `gunbc.design_ruling::claim_execution_has_one_v1_entrypoint`."),
    ]),
    h2(text: "1. Intention"),
    p(text: "**What:** callers name the claims they want through one interface, `gunbc test <target-pattern>...`, and every invocation's result is derived by one rule. The `claim_batch` binary and `gunbc run --claim-run` are deleted, and every executing caller is in the form it keeps after the seed is gone."),
    p(text: "**The durable part and the temporary part.** What survives the seed: the caller migration, the label grammar, the execution options and the meaning of a result. What is temporary: the seed's implementation of them. The native compiler later implements the same contract wherever it can faithfully replace seed execution; when the seed disappears, callers should already be in their final form. This needs no new executor framework: most of the contract is already `gunbc.target_invocation`, and the interpreted entrypoints already share `run_claim_measured`. The work consolidates the selection, classification and reporting around it."),
    p(text: "**The contract.** Callers name claims by label. The existing authorities decide which claims and which execution route those names denote (`gunbc.target_invocation` `admit_test_operand`, `gunbc.discovery_census` `claim_route_universe`). Every selected claim has one located outcome, and a failure to establish the selection stays explicit. One rule, `gunbc.target_invocation` `claim_route_termination` over `ClaimRouteVerdict`, derives the result. The seed carries a hand mirror of that rule; agreement between the two is checked by execution, which is a mitigation and not structural elimination of disagreement."),
    p(text: "**Why (operator, 2026-11-22):** three seed entrypoints evaluate claims through the same `run_claim_measured`, each with its own argument grammar and its own reading of the outcome, so the same witness can read red, unreached or absent depending on which tool ran it. That is a meaning fork in the most trusted channel the repository has, not only duplicated code, and every caller and reviewer pays to know which reading they are looking at."),
    p(text: "**This is v1 work and is admitted on that footing.** The seed is semantics-frozen and maintenance-active (`gunbc.v1.v1_maintenance_standing::v1_seed_standing`). Claim execution stays out of CI until the native frontier clears (`gunbc.design_ruling::no_ci_claim_execution_until_native_frontier_clears`); nothing here changes that, and the evidence for this change is executed locally or on a fleet host, never claimed as required-CI enforcement. The change is mostly deletion (`BehaviorPreservingRedundancyRemoval`) plus one adapter repair (`DefectRepairDiagnosticsMayMove`). Repeated operands and an execution-mode operand on `gunbc test` are `PublicSurfaceGrowth`, admitted only inside the same change that deletes the two larger surfaces they replace, under the operator's ruling."),
    h2(text: "2. Done when"),
    p(text: "Each is assessed against the tree unless marked as the operator's judgement."),
    ul(items: [
      li(text: "**Every named caller has a disposition, and no capability is lost.** Each executing caller in section 3 is one of: *migrated* (the new invocation produces the observation its consumer needs, with the correct execution provenance); *retired* (the consumer or its requirement is obsolete, so the removal is intentional); or *blocked on native support* (the required observation cannot yet be preserved). A deletion a blocked caller depends on waits for that support, and until then the old route stays frozen: no new callers, no new options. Recording a gap does not discharge a disposition."),
      li(text: "**No `//v2/...` label is sent to the interpreter.** That universe is the native route's (`gunbc.target_invocation` `admit_test_operand`), and an interpreted result cannot stand in for a native one. A seed-executed witness *about* v2, whose consumer needs a particular claim evaluated, may be relabelled or relocated where that accurately states its role; a witness establishing *native execution* is not given interpreter evidence."),
      li(text: "**One invocation runs an exact supplied batch.** `gunbc test` accepts several operands and runs exactly the claims they denote, in one process, sharing preparation where its inputs and lifetime permit. Overlapping operands select each claim identity once. No caller widens a sparse request to `:all` or a subtree to fit the interface, and none spawns one process per claim. The child-process boundary that bounds retained memory (`gunbc.instruments.host_prelude`) is kept."),
      li(text: "**No silent change of source universe.** For each caller that supplies source roots today, it is established whether that set is redundant with `witness_layer_roots` or meaningful (fixture-driven callers especially), and the migration preserves the meaningful ones."),
      li(text: "**Results are constructed, then rendered.** The selected identities are established once; each receives exactly one outcome; the printed lines and the exit status are both derived from that one collection. A known selected claim that cannot execute gets an unobserved outcome with its cause. A source whose claims cannot be enumerated is reported as a source or selection failure; no claim identity is invented for it. Success requires all of: selection completed with no unresolved failure, a nonempty selection, exactly one outcome per selected identity, and every outcome held. Recoverable entry or claim failures do not stop the independently runnable claims; a failure that prevents trustworthy selection leaves the invocation explicitly incomplete."),
      li(text: "**The existing verdict policy, realized correctly.** Held is `ClaimHeld`; false or a non-Bool return is `ClaimDidNotHold`; a runtime error, host refusal, unwind or budget interrupt is `ClaimUnobserved`; any did-not-hold gives exit 1, otherwise any unobserved member or an empty selection gives exit 2, otherwise 0. The seed adapter `claim_route_verdict` stops classifying every `ExitFailure` as did-not-hold: a claim's typed `ProcessExit` failure with code 2 is unobserved. That reading belongs to the typed claim-result boundary; an arbitrary host command's exit code is not a claim-runner protocol result."),
      li(text: "**Execution mode is an invocation option.** It reuses `std.execution_mode::ExecutionMode` (Hermetic by default, Wet, Record with a fixture store), selected through the seed's shared `execution_mode_for`, as the caller's authority to permit live effects. A combination a route cannot honour (a mode on the native or instrument route) refuses explicitly; no route ignores it."),
      li(text: "**Deleted spellings are separated from kept behaviour.** `--eval-budget-ms`, `--outcomes-out`, `--print-entry-closure` and `--pre-push` are deleted only where no named caller depends on what they did: removing `--eval-budget-ms` changes no execution bound that is enforced today, removing `--outcomes-out` loses no result detail another consumer reads from ordinary output, and a closure query with no retained consumer gets no replacement command. A measurement line survives only where a consumer or the cost comparison reads it."),
      li(text: "**Discriminating cases execute the real adapter and invocation path,** not only the model's pure fold: held, false and unobserved; false together with unobserved (exit 1, both outcomes reported); an empty selection; an `ExitFailure` with code 2; A holds, B cannot resolve, C holds (A and C run, B is located, exit is not 0); and a duplicated outcome for A cannot satisfy B's obligation."),
      li(text: "**No repeated closure construction, unrelated discovery work or material resource regression.** Compared under comparable conditions for preparation work, wall time and peak memory: one exact label against `claim_batch` on the same entry (proposed: `github_pull_request_decode_witness`, from the `gunbc.plans.closure_consolidation` measurement table), and one representative existing pooled request with its selected identities and inputs preserved. A single timing is a sample, so the reading is against noise, not a literal no-greater. Any exact-label optimization keeps the discovery admission rules."),
      li(text: "No `claim_batch` binary is declared in `src/v1/stage0/Cargo.toml`, no `--claim-run` option is in the `gunbc run` dispatch surface, and no executing caller in section 3 spawns either, unless a caller is blocked on native support and the route it needs is frozen as stated above. Judged by a cited grep over dag, src and .github at the landing revision, stating what it inspected; it is not a semantic absence proof."),
      li(text: "Operator's judgement: a contributor asking how to run one witness, or ten, is given one command."),
    ]),
    h2(text: "3. Observation, read at 00de8d4c88d"),
    p(text: "Read from source at that revision on 2026-11-22: `src/v1/stage0/src/bin/claim_batch.rs`, `src/v1/stage0/src/target_invocation_host.rs` (`test_verb`, `claim_route_verdict`, `run_claim_route`), `src/v1/stage0/src/cli_run.rs` (`run_claim_route`, `run_claim`) and `dag/gunbc/target_invocation.dag`; callers by `git grep` for the binary name, its environment variable and its flags over dag, src and .github. The grep finds shapes, not facts; what it did not inspect is unknown, and the caller list below is a bounded candidate set, not a census."),
    ul(items: [
      li(text: "**Three entrypoints, one evaluator.** `claim_batch` (`--entry` plus `--function`/`--functions`), `gunbc test <pattern>` (one operand; claim route under `//test/claim/...`), and `gunbc run --claim-run` (`--entry` plus repeatable `--function`) all reach `run_claim_measured` and `run_claim`. The floor fold (`reach_base_standings`) also calls the evaluator and is not a command-line entrypoint."),
      li(text: "**The model is right and the seed adapter is not.** `gunbc.target_invocation` already has the three-way verdict and its aggregation. The seed's `claim_route_verdict` maps every `ExitFailure` to did-not-hold, code 2 included. Separately, `claim_batch` maps a runtime error, unwind, budget interrupt and unresolved host tool to FAIL and exit 1, against the model's unobserved."),
      li(text: "**Completeness.** A resolve failure is one group's UNOBSERVED lines under `claim_batch` and aborts the whole claim route with no per-claim lines. `gunbc run --claim-run` reported 13 of 13 for an entry declaring 14 (`gunbc.recurring_failure_mode::a_claim_that_runtime_errors_is_dropped_as_no_verdict_rather_than_red`)."),
      li(text: "**Pooling.** `gunbc.instruments.host_prelude` `claim_batch_claims_argv_route` sends a supplied list of entry and function pairs, with its own source roots, through one `claim_batch` child, which its comments justify against the earlier one-cold-process-per-claim cost; the claim route takes one operand and supplies `witness_layer_roots` itself."),
      li(text: "**Executing callers found:** `gunbc.instruments.host_prelude`, `gunbc.instruments.merge_admission_capture_transport`, `gunbc.instruments.known_red_derivation`, `gunbc.instruments.interp_recorded_fixture_witness_transport` and the `interp_recorded_fixture_witness` binary (`--record`, `--hermetic`, `--fixture-store`), `gunbc.offline_local_recipe`, `gunbc.compute.work_provider_local` and the `ClaimBatchRunner` binary in `gunbc.compute.work_request` and `std.materialization_provider`, `gunbc.roadmap.roadmap_belt_actuate`, `gunbc.devboot.program`, `src/v1/stage0/src/pre_push.rs` (spawns `claim_batch` with `--claim-run`), the release-binary rosters (`gunbc.ci.ci_release_bins`, `fleet-converge.yml`), and `claim_batch`'s own witnesses. No executing caller was found for `--eval-budget-ms`, `--print-entry-closure`, or `--outcomes-out` beyond its own witness."),
      li(text: "**Population.** The claim route's universe is `//test/claim/...` (`dag/test/claim`). A `src/v2/test/claim` claim has a `//v2/...` label and routes to the native test route. A test function in a module outside both universes has no `gunbc test` route; `claim_batch` reaches any entry it is handed."),
      li(text: "**Cost shape.** Both pay the module index and the entry closure resolve; the claim route also resolves the floor discovery producer entry, narrowed to the modules the pattern can reach. Measured `claim_batch` runs in the `gunbc.plans.closure_consolidation` before-and-after table (srv1, shared box, wall from `/usr/bin/time -v`): about 3 min 50 s and 7 GiB for `github_pull_request_decode_witness`, about 19 min and 15.6 GiB for `compiler_gate_workflow_witness`. Cost follows the entry's closure, not the number of claims in it."),
    ]),
    h2(text: "4. Questions settled by reading the named callers"),
    p(text: "These are engineering questions answered from the callers in section 3, not choices put to the operator unless the reading finds a genuine tradeoff."),
    ul(items: [
      li(text: "**`src/v2/test/claim` claims a caller evaluates through `claim_batch` today.** For each, whether its consumer needs that claim evaluated (relabel or relocate it where that states its role accurately) or needs native-execution evidence (it waits for native support, and the route it uses stays frozen)."),
      li(text: "**Test functions outside `//test/claim/...` a caller evaluates.** Decided from each function's role: its semantic home really is `test.claim` and it moves; or it belongs to an already registered exact target; or the admission model needs a narrow correction to express a legitimate supported request. No production module is moved, no internal interface is exposed, and no duplicate wrapper claim is added only to fit the router."),
      li(text: "**Source roots,** per caller, as stated in section 2."),
      li(text: "**Exact-label discovery,** whether an exact label may skip part of the discovery producer resolve while keeping what establishes that the named function is a claim."),
    ]),
    h2(text: "5. Realization"),
    p(text: "Not authored here. The work items that realize this intention name it when they are staffed and may be redrawn without this plan changing."),
  ]
}

data claim_execution_consolidation_plan: Plan = Plan {
  projection: PlanIsAuthorityOnly,
  slug: "claim-execution-consolidation",
  title: "Claim execution consolidation: one claim interface, one result rule",
  body: claim_execution_consolidation_body(),
  retirement: PlanRetiresWhen { condition: unbound_dissolution(description: "Section 2 is achieved: every done-when condition holds on the tree, or for the judgement condition the operator has accepted it. The contract this plan establishes outlives it: the native compiler implements the same interface and result rule, and this plan is not retired by the seed's deletion alone.") },
}
